---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import LegalNotice from '../components/LegalNotice.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use"
  description={`The terms that apply when you use the ${site.name} website, resources and forms.`}
  crumbs={[
    { label: 'Home', href: '/' },
    { label: 'Terms of Use' },
  ]}
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container page-hero-inner">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        The basic rules for using this website, downloading resources and
        submitting information through our forms.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container legal-page">
    <LegalNotice />
    {/* TODO: Have these terms reviewed by a qualified Indian legal professional. */}

    <div class="prose">
      <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> {site.legal.lastUpdated}</p>

      <h2>1. Acceptance</h2>
      <p>
        By using this website, you agree to these terms. If you do not agree,
        please do not use the site. These terms apply to visitors, candidates,
        employers and anyone who downloads a resource.
      </p>

      <h2>2. About the site</h2>
      <p>
        {site.name} is a marketing and analytics careers brand operated in
        {site.legal.jurisdiction}. The site provides educational resources, a
        newsletter, a talent network and a way for employers to contact us. It is
        not a job board, an employment agency guarantee, a university or a
        regulated adviser.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Use of the website</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Use the site lawfully and do not attempt to disrupt or damage it.</li>
        <li>Do not scrape, copy or republish substantial parts of the site without permission.</li>
        <li>Do not submit false, misleading or unlawful information through our forms.</li>
        <li>Do not use the site to harass anyone or to send spam.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Resources and intellectual property</h2>
      <p>
        Unless stated otherwise, the text, design, graphics and downloadable
        resources on this site belong to {site.name} or are used with permission.
        You may download and use free resources for your own personal,
        non-commercial learning. Do not sell them, remove attribution or present
        them as your own work. For permission to use material commercially,
        contact us.
      </p>

      <h2>5. No guarantees</h2>
      <p>
        We do not guarantee interviews, job offers, placements, promotions,
        salary levels, income, training outcomes or any other career result.
        Career decisions are yours, and hiring decisions are made by employers.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Candidates and employers</h2>
      <p>
        Candidates are never charged a fee for joining the talent network,
        introductions or placements. Employers may be charged a success fee,
        which is agreed in writing before work begins. Submitting a form does not
        create an employment, agency or client relationship. We may decline a
        brief or a candidate at our discretion.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Information you submit</h2>
      <p>
        Do not submit confidential information that you are not allowed to share.
        By submitting a form, you confirm that the information is accurate and
        that you have the right to share it. Our handling of personal information
        is described in the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Third-party services and links</h2>
      <p>
        We use third-party services for hosting, forms, newsletter delivery and
        optional analytics. We may link to other websites. We do not control
        third-party services and are not responsible for their content, security
        or practices. Their terms and policies apply to your use of them.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Educational content</h2>
      <p>
        Articles and resources are educational. They are not career, legal,
        financial or professional advice, and they may not fit your specific
        situation. See the <a href="/disclaimer/">disclaimer</a> for more detail.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the extent permitted by law, {site.name} and its operator are not
        liable for indirect, incidental or consequential loss arising from your
        use of the site, its resources or its forms. Nothing in these terms
        excludes liability that cannot lawfully be excluded.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Changes to the site and terms</h2>
      <p>
        We may change, suspend or remove parts of the site at any time. We may
        update these terms as the brand grows. The "last updated" date will
        change when we do. Continued use of the site after a change means you
        accept the updated terms.
      </p>

      <h2>12. Governing law</h2>
      <p>
        These terms are governed by the laws of {site.legal.jurisdiction}. Subject
        to applicable law, the courts at {site.legal.city} have jurisdiction over
        disputes connected with the site.
      </p>
      {/* TODO: Confirm the governing-law city with your legal reviewer. */}

      <h2>13. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these terms? Email
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
